WEBVTT

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:36.320
Hello... you must be tired after the long flight.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.240
The mansion you'll be investigating in this fores–

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:48.880
Hi... Hi... Hirato-san, you idiot!

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.300
Thank you for helping out with the show.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.550
From what I've heard, there were all kinds of blunders.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.560
According to this report based on the surveys done by the citizens,

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.520
the nature of the play was questionable.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.440
Nyanperona was acting out of character... and well,
these are just some of the examples cited.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.160
Still, it's commendable that no one was injured.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.950
Members of the First Ship would like to thank you guys.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.750
I want you to go to Rinoll, the Ice Crystal Town.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.580
"Have a break", while you carry out the additional investigations.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.340
Consider it a <i>reward.</i>

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:40.100
What was that kind smile all about?!
What was that kind smile all about?!

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.680
Silvery Box
Score 8
What was that kind smile all about?!
What was that kind smile all about?!

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.100
Score 8
Silvery Box

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.480
A moment please.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.110
This is something from the Second Ship's Captain.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.230
Eh? Something from Hirato-san?

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.320
I wonder what's inside.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:02.620
Huh? It's empty.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.000
A snowman?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.000
Snowman?

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:17.340
Yukkin, a warm snowman created by the design team at the Research Tower.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.760
Yukkin?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.220
Yukkin!

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.470
Yukkin!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.350
So... So cute!

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.310
It's so warm!

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:42.570
Hirato-san... Does he care about us or not?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.580
I don't understand Hirato-san at all!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.580
<i>Seeing as to how he's letting us travel together, I suppose we're just going to be bait again.</i>

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:56.590
<i>I'm not satisfied with just smelling the smoke.</i>

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:03.300
<i>That idiot hiding within the smoke, basking in his sense of superiority as he watches people cry...</i>

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.310
<i>If this can allow me to seize him by the collar, I'll play along and let them use me.</i>

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.890
Sorry, Gareki-kun.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:10.770
What?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.640
You were feeling cold, weren't you?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.650
You were blowing in your hands, Gareki.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.320
I don't need a snowman.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.530
Let the girl and brat hold it.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:26.120
I'm older than Gareki by a year, so you don't have to hold back.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.370
Just let Nai hold on to it, will you!

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.590
Ga-Gareki-kun... It's wrong! You're using it wrong! It hurts...

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:37.840
Well then, I'll be on standby back at the lodging.
Ga-Gareki-kun... It's wrong! You're using it wrong! It hurts...

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.760
Ga-Gareki.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:48.770
I strongly question your decision to let him move around so freely.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.390
There are a few known examples of captured Niji,

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:57.030
believed to be the same kind of species that Nai is formed from, because of its rare existence.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:00.860
All experiments in breeding them have failed.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:07.410
Since sounds in their natural environment are related to sustaining their lives,

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:12.500
we presume that being kept in a closed area creates large amounts of stress on it.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:17.800
For this reason, I feel that the current situation is the best way to supervise Nai.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:22.220
We received a report that he was almost abducted by Kafka!

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:26.630
The Research Tower and Circus have different objectives in handling Nai.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:32.010
The Research Tower views him as an important specimen to advance technology.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:38.900
But for us, he's a mysterious dancer who's able to bring Varuga to us.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:44.360
I hope you understand that the encounters with Varuga and the dangers associated with them

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.660
are part of the role that we imposed on him.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.910
I believe that you worry that if he's taken away, there will be disadvantages...

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.160
If that ever happens,

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.910
I'll kill him with my own hands.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.250
Wait, Hirato!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.090
You're right about Nai's value as only an experiment specimen to me.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:11.350
But taking a life is not something you should decide at your own convenience.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.310
You're such a saint.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:16.850
What do you mean?

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.690
You belong to those that protect lives,

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.030
and I to those that take them away.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.820
A difference of opinions between us is inevitable.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:34.500
The phrase “feigned politeness” exists for someone like you.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.750
Hey, hey, you guys are really…

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.960
Who do you think you're talking to, Tsukitachi?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.970
Compared to Hirato's feigned politeness, you're just plain rude!

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.340
Please don't take it out on me, Akari-chan.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.880
I'll excuse myself then, Akari-san.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:55.890
Well, he may come off hard-headed, but he's actually quite kind-hearted on the inside.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:00.270
I don't believe he wants to kill Nai.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.360
Think about what he said earlier.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.650
I don't think the higher-ups were too happy about it.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.370
"What a short-sighted idea. To think that killing him would solve everything".

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:16.040
It's more beneficial to keep Nai alive.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:21.040
"Therefore I think we should hold back the opinion to dissect Nai".

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.960
"I suppose those opinions to dissect him began surfacing because they were having...

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.760
a hard time decoding Karoku's notebook".

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:31.600
Don't worry.

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:33.970
Someone's always following Nai.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:36.940
Besides, we've also attached a transmitter to his bracelet.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:44.860
Let's go.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.610
Yukkin, this way.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.620
<i>Yukki. Yukki. Yu.</i>

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:52.860
Love.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.080
He's such an idiot.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:06.840
This mansion somehow gives me the creeps.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:13.890
Well, this vacation house is owned by an executive officer

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:17.470
of a Kafka-related company, which the First Ship busted.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.060
What exactly are we looking for?

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.230
To confirm if anything was left out of the search when this place was busted.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.980
It's just a follow-up to check things out.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:30.400
To see if there are still documents or drugs remaining that are related to Kafka.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.030
Nai-chan, aren't you cold?

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.110
Huh?

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:41.210
I'm sorry. Hirato-san was probably thinking that you could play with the snow

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:44.750
once the blizzard was gone.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.540
Snow is fun.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.760
It was so fluffy and squishy.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:52.050
It was lots of fun, right?

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:54.930
Really?

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:59.850
Yeah. The feeling of my feet sinking was new to me.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:04.350
<i>By any chance, was this Gareki-kun's first time experiencing snow?</i>

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.820
<i>He was saying those words unconsciously, wasn't he?</i>

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.110
<i>That's so adorable.</i>

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:17.040
All right! Let's work hard and spend the last day playing!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.370
Yay!

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.420
In the end, there was nothing there.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.670
It's not really a bad thing that we didn't find anything.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.430
Yukkin is gone.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:47.440
<i>Yukki. Yukki. Yukki. Yu-</i>

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:51.320
Hey, there really is something here.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.940
What? Did you find a rare item?

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:58.330
<i>Yu…Yu…Yukki.</i>

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:02.950
I'm going back to the mansion, so everyone else should head back to the lodging–

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:06.170
Nai, listen carefully for that snowman's voice.

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:08.920
It's already going to be difficult to hear its voice,

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.420
because the snow muffles sound.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.710
Sure, I'll do my best.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:21.140
Yogi, let's hurry.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.310
Okay, Tsukumo-chan.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.730
Awesome! It's so warm!

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:35.400
At this rate, we can play with it for two more hours.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.490
This is an item from the Second Ship of Circus.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.410
I've never seen this before so it must be a rare item.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.160
Then that means Circus is here.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.380
Yahoo!

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:52.130
Aren't we competent for getting rid of all of the evidence just before they came?

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:52.960
Yahoo!

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.800
We covered everything up. Right, Kiharu?

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.380
It's amazing! Magnificent! Gorgeous!

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.340
If there is anything we missed, Uro-san will kill us.
It's amazing! Magnificent! Gorgeous!

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.630
If there is anything we missed, Uro-san will kill us.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.930
Let's just kill Circus with our momentum!

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.770
Don't get so excited.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.430
It's such a pain.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:14.940
But, if I can get some limited-edition Circus items, I'm game.

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.190
Shall we do it?

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.040
A sound?

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.330
I wonder if he fell into this hole.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:31.960
I'll go take a look.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.960
Yogi, I'll go too.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:37.590
Right, lend me your ears, Nai-chan.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.100
Be careful.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:53.520
I can't see very well in this darkness, but it seems to be man-made.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.950
Yukkin! Are you here?

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.400
I hear sounds from over there.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:05.830
Gareki-kun?

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:16.510
Owwww. I'm sorry, Gareki-kun.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:21.890
Tsukumo-chan, stay there in case of an emergency.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:31.600
This is a man-made hole.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.610
There's a door.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:44.330
This place is under the mansion, isn't it?

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.290
Right.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.710
You two stay behind me, since I can't tell what will happen.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.150
There it is!
There it is!
There it is!

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:14.150
It hurts! Dammit!

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:14.650
It's there. I don't want to go anymore. Let's go home.
It hurts! Dammit!

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:17.230
You idiot, look carefully. It's just a doll.
It's there. I don't want to go anymore. Let's go home.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:23.440
Hey, Nai-chan, wait!

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.030
Don't touch it!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:28.490
Stop it!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:40.800
The box... something's shaking inside?

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.260
Yukkin.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.350
Yukkin!

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.520
I'm so glad.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.440
Where have you been?

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:01.570
We were all looking for you.
<i>Yuukkin.</i>

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.740
Look, that girl is a member of Circus.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:09.950
Of course. She was looking into the hole where we found that white dango.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.700
It's so obvious, Kagiri-san.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.750
You're an idiot, Kiharu.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:19.210
If she was just an ordinarily person, we would've broken the promise with Uro-san

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.420
to not attract attention to ourselves.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:24.090
Then it'll be bad even if we encounter members of Circus, right?

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:27.550
But Kiharu, we're going to kill her, aren't we?

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:37.520
In that case, we'll make sure even the dead can't talk. We'll be commended for killing Circus.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.940
<i>I couldn't sense him approaching.</i>

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.530
<i>Could he be?</i>

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:46.360
Tsukumo-chan, sorry for keeping you waiting!

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.320
Kiharu.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.530
She had companions!

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:54.870
Yogi!

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:59.500
Are you two okay?

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.340
Yes.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:01.830
Mm-hm.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.460
Something must've happened above.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.340
I have to save Tsukumo-chan!

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.340
Wait.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.680
Don't waste your energy.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:15.010
Wha–? Why are you carrying such a thing?

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.890
I found them at the mansion.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.770
So what? You took them? You don't call that–

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:20.520
Let's go back to that doll room.
So what? You took them? You don't call that–

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.770
Let's go back to that doll room.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:43.580
Tsukumo-chan!

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:49.550
Yogi, that was…

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.760
Sorry to surprise you.

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:57.430
Gareki-kun made a bomb out of things we found underground.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.560
Hey, don't ignore us!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.690
Varuga!

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:12.330
Tsukumo-chan.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.120
Nai-kun.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.630
It hurts!

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.500
Come on this way. You're so lame.

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:32.510
Wai– Look at the clothes the black-haired guy's wearing.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:35.810
The special thermal coats that only the Research Tower personnel wear!

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:39.060
Tsukumo-chan, take Nai-chan somewhere safe.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.140
It's not in my collection!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.350
But…
It's not in my collection!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:42.060
It's not in my collection!

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.560
A super rare item!

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:48.190
Take care of him until we group up with you later.

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.530
<i>Are they after Nai-chan again?</i>

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:01.120
Gareki-kun, I'll protect you, so do as I say...

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.790
Hey you, stop standing in front of me!

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.250
You're getting in my way!

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.300
Hey, I'm protecting you!

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:12.840
I'm a member of Circus, and you're just a normal boy, get it?

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.800
This is my duty.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:18.770
Not only that, I don't want my friend to get hurt...

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.100
Come again?

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.520
Your friend?

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:23.100
In what way?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.850
<i>He's dead serious!</i>

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:28.480
W-Well,

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:33.200
<i>I see... Am I the only one to think that?</i>

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:38.080
<i>Come to think of it, I don't recall Gareki-kun ever calling me by my name..</i>

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:42.500
<i>What? Maybe he dislikes me?</i>

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:47.090
Hey, I'm old enough to tell the difference between our abilities to fight.

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:50.000
But I'm not useless either.

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:54.010
Wha– You're right. I'm sorry.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.390
I'll provide you with support.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:56.680
Do your best.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:58.010
Okay, sure!

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:02.390
Filled with the power of man's spirit.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:05.140
I'm the Sparkling Prince who makes your hearts throb!

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:11.900
The Second Ship Fighter of the National Defense Organization, Circus, Yogi.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.900
Let's fight!

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:17.740
I'm sorry, it's my fault.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.910
No, it's not Tsukumo-chan's fault.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.870
Thanks for saving me just now.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.410
I was very happy.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:27.910
But you mustn't get hurt, Nai-kun.

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:33.300
I was so scared that you may have been hurt badly.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:37.510
I… I want to be strong like you, Tsukumo-chan.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.550
Can I be strong?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:44.230
Nai-kun, you have a very strong soul.

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:48.060
You've gone through so much, yet you've never been discouraged.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:52.060
I think it's great that you can be kind to others at all times.

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:55.490
I feel relaxed when I'm with you, Nai-kun.

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:58.900
I'm sure everyone, including Karoku-san, feels the same way.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:03.160
So let us return home safely.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.130
Because you're telling me not to damage the black-haired boy's clothes,

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.130
I can't go all out.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:19.050
Hold it– Shouldn't we kill the ones that got away?

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:23.350
There's nothing interesting about those two!

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.600
However, this encounter gives us better items!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.520
<i>They're not after Nai-chan?</i>

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:34.610
Hey, what kind of person is your boss?

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:35.770
Come again?

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:38.490
I'm asking you what kind of person he is.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.120
<i>Ah, I see.</i>

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:45.460
<i>It's understandable that Gareki-kun doesn't like me.</i>

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:48.750
<i>I couldn't save Yotaka-kun.</i>

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:52.130
Are you talking about our boss, Uro-san?

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:55.800
He'll get pissed at me if he sees us fighting so pathetically...

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.720
Say, can I go on a rampage?

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:00.630
I give up. You're such a pain in the neck.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:02.130
It's time for the real fight.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.890
Let's show them our true powers!

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:06.430
<i>Rasudan Bug!</i>

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:17.530
You lost your eyesight temporarily due to the special rhythm of light signals

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.730
being transmitted to your brain.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:25.200
Hey, handsome lil' guy!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.580
Gareki-kun, say something–

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.250
Yogi–

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:42.130
Hey, be quiet.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:44.630
Gareki-kun, where are you?!

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.030
Oh? Why, I haven't dealt the finishing blow yet...

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.570
Ga..re...

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.580
I can finally see–

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:33.310
Let's do something fun. Something awesome...

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:41.530
I'll be very happy if everyone laughs as if they're screaming.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.790
Yogi!
Yogi!
Yogi!

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:28.840
Tsukumo-senpai, will you be transferred to Rinoll?

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.180
I will be conducting an investigation over there.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:32.590
Please don't forget about me.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:34.600
It'll only be for a short time, so I won't forget you.

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:37.140
I'm so very sad.

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:39.230
Thank you, Kiichi-chan.
